---
version: 2.0.2
title: root help
file: ./test/licence_audit/output_snapshot_test.gleam
test_name: root_help_test
---
Report locked dependency licences by default, or select a command. Use --help
(alias: -h) for help.

Report Hex package licences without enforcing policy findings. Operational
failures exit 2. Use `check` to enforce a licence policy.

USAGE:
    licence_audit ( check | notices | report | sbom | update | vulns ) [
        --cache-dir=<DIR> --color=<auto|always|never> --config=<PATH>
        --ignore-config --manifest=<PATH> --no-cache --quiet --scope=<prod|all>
        --verbose --version ]

FLAGS:
    --cache-dir=<DIR>            Use DIR as the application cache root for all
                                 cache families

    --color=<auto|always|never>  Colorize output: auto|always|never (default
                                 auto; alias: --colour)

    --config=<PATH>              Read configuration from PATH

    --help                       Print help information

    --ignore-config              Ignore configuration files

    --manifest=<PATH>            Read manifest from PATH

    --no-cache                   Bypass the on-disk caches

    --quiet                      Suppress progress output (alias: -q)

    --scope=<prod|all>           Dependency scope: prod|all (production only or
                                 all dependencies)

    --verbose                    Show detailed progress output (alias: -v)

    --version                    Print the installed version (alias: -V)

SUBCOMMANDS:
    check                 Enforce selected checks: licences (default), vulns, or all.
    notices               Generate a release-ready `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`-style file from locked dependencies.
    report                Report Hex package licences without enforcing policy findings.
    sbom                  Generate a CycloneDX 1.6 or SPDX 2.3 JSON SBOM from manifest.toml.
    update                Review discovered licences and update [tools.licence_audit].
    vulns                 Report known vulnerabilities for locked dependencies using the OSV.dev database.

